Subject: [PATCH 09025/11362] Fix the conductor's determination restore: it was
 blind to downgrade, only caught deletion

ITEM 1 of the operator's "move 1 + 2 + 3". REQ-OPS-DETERMINATION-RESTORE-6260.

The 2026-08-12 incident had a cause I misattributed. I reported it as "the
conductor commits --no-verify so the lint never runs". True but incomplete: a
self-heal for exactly this already existed and already ran before every conductor
`git add -A`. It restored NOTHING, because its test was `k not in cur` -- False
when the key is PRESENT and merely nulled, and the damage was
`flagged_adversarial: True -> None`. The guard ran and was silently non-firing on
the one case it was written for. That is the SILENT_NON_FIRING class CLAUDE.md's
QA-Layer discipline names, and it describes the incident better than the
--no-verify framing did.

Widened: a determination is meaningful only when TRUTHY, since False and None both
re-admit a quarantined artifact to headline aggregation, so truthy-in-HEAD and
falsy-or-absent-now is damage. Still strictly additive, so it cannot lose a
legitimate edit, and a deliberate clear expressed the sanctioned way -- falsy value
PLUS a `*_cleared_note` -- is left alone.

The decision rule is extracted as the pure function `determination_damage` so it
can be pinned without a git fixture. 8 tests: both damage shapes, the
deliberate-clear carve-out, falsy-in-HEAD, non-determination keys, and fresh
measurements alongside a lost determination. A first attempt drove the real helper
through a throwaway git repo and kept failing while the helper provably worked --
`run_cmd` pins cwd=PROJECT_ROOT -- so testing the rule directly is both simpler and
a better test of what actually changed.

Also clears a FALSE-POSITIVE fabrication flag on exp6250, the session's one
positive result. TAUTOLOGY fired on rex_pooled_mean_held ==
best_pure_arm_pooled_mean_held == 0.481, but this experiment computes best_pure =
max(linear, rex) and rex was the larger arm, so the two cannot differ. Cleared
per-artifact with an auditable `*_cleared_note`; corrigendum_pending retained per
never-prune. A general derived-extremum carve-out was attempted in
adversarial_verify.py and REVERTED: the sibling match pulled in
ensemble_pooled_mean_held, which is not a pure arm, so the verified-max test
failed. A name-inference heuristic that misfires on its first real case does not
belong in a fabrication gate.

